  "upload": {
    "title": "How Samsung Makes Glass Fold in Half 🤯 #shorts",
    "description": "The Galaxy Z Fold8 Ultra's inner screen uses ultra-thin glass (UTG) that is thin enough to flex, backed by Samsung's new Flex Titanium layer (a titanium-alloy film plus a titanium plate) that supports the display and reduces crease visibility. Unfolded, the phone is 4.1 mm thin. Samsung says the crease is less visible than ever, but after a week of daily use Tom's Guide found the 'crease-free' display settled into a visible rut, especially under bright light. Price: from $2,099.",
